From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm: verisilicon: accept RGB888 on the BT1120 HDMI bridge

Linux 6.18's SII902x bridge participates in atomic bus-format negotiation
and requests MEDIA_BUS_FMT_RGB888_1X24 for its parallel input.  The X5
BT1120 bridge already selects RGB888 as its online input format, but its
output-format filter only accepts FIXED and packed YUV formats.  Consequently
every HDMI atomic modeset fails with -ENOTSUPP.

Accept RGB888 as a valid output format for the online BT1120-to-SII902x path.
The older vendor kernel did not expose this because its SII902x driver skipped
input bus-format negotiation and passed MEDIA_BUS_FMT_FIXED instead.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/verisilicon/dc_bt1120/bt1120_bridge.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/verisilicon/dc_bt1120/bt1120_bridge.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/verisilicon/dc_bt1120/bt1120_bridge.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/verisilicon/dc_bt1120/bt1120_bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/verisilicon/dc_bt1120/bt1120_bridge.c
@@ -131,6 +131,7 @@ static u32 *bt1120_bridge_get_input_bus_fmts(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 		bt1120->is_online = true;
 
 	switch (output_fmt) {
+	case MEDIA_BUS_FMT_RGB888_1X24:
 	case MEDIA_BUS_FMT_FIXED:
 	case MEDIA_BUS_FMT_UYVY8_1X16:
 	case MEDIA_BUS_FMT_VYUY8_1X16:
-- 
